ready: 1
kind: journey
id: retention.forget
display_id: FLOW-RETENTION-FORGET
module: retention
actors: [actor.owner]
title: Forget or delete a memory
summary: The owner forgets a memory reversibly, recovers it, or purges it for good after reviewing everything the purge removes.
trigger: The owner wants a memory out of the agent's view, or gone
steps:
  - retention.forget.choose
  - retention.forget.forgotten
  - retention.forget.recover
  - retention.forget.pick
  - retention.forget.preview
  - retention.forget.purged
  - retention.forget.cancelled
  - retention.forget.no-terminal
  - retention.forget.not-found
sequences:
  - retention.seq.forget
  - retention.seq.recover
  - retention.seq.purge
rationale: >-
  The preview reminds the owner that runtimes keep their own transcripts:
  Kernle can only promise deletion of what it holds, and the owner may need the
  runtime's own controls as well.
